## Data quality & method

- Victim data: ransomware.live leak-site aggregation; {{ dq.cross_rate }} of records in the window were independently confirmed by a second leak-site scraper (RansomLook / ransomwatch; name + group match within ±7 days).
- Sector attribution: {{ dq.sector_source }}% from the aggregator, {{ dq.sector_keyword }}% keyword-inferred, {{ dq.sector_llm }}% LLM-inferred, {{ dq.sector_unknown }}% unknown. Size band known for {{ dq.size_known }}% of in-scope victims.
- Leak-site posts are claims by criminals; victims are not verified and posting dates lag intrusions by weeks. IAB figures come from public articles, not from forums, so they describe what researchers chose to report.
- Sources: ransomware.live (Julien Mousqueton, CC BY-NC-SA), RansomLook (ransomlook.io), ransomwatch (joshhighet), and the public RSS feeds configured in scope.yaml. Generated by the CTI Ops platform (P6 pipeline).
